Tracks 1-4, 6 and 7 first change inside the engine's 2-second hold; track 5 first changes after it (the late-discovery case).
What decoding changed (every track changes 31147 samples); track 1: 31147 of 793800 samples (3.92%); the other 762653 decoded to exactly sample x 32768, the level of a decode with no effect. No decoded sample exceeded the 16-bit range (largest |value| is 32767 x 32768).
  Samples at or above the Peak Extend threshold (|x| >= 0x5981): 9115; 9108 of them decoded to exactly sample x 32768 and 7 changed, by at most 0.8% (for example 25206 to 25404.27 in 16-bit units). Gain adjustment is exercised heavily by this disc; Peak Extend is flagged in its packets but barely changes any sample.
  31140 of the 31147 changed values have a bit set below 2^11 (15417 also have bit 0 set), so they are libhdcd's full-precision gain results, not values on a 20-bit grid. The render callback converts the 32-bit ring to Float32, which holds 24 significant bits, so a value with finer detail than that is rounded there.

