=== Addendum: the owner's listening check, the display fix and the ordinary-CD control (2026-11-03, evening) ===
The blocks above are unchanged. This addendum records the owner's listening check in the Release app, the display bug it exposed, the fix with its test and re-test, and an ordinary-CD control. The first listening ran on a Release app built from commit 39127c6, which has the code of the M8.4 commit 852732f. The fix, its test and everything after it were done in the working tree on top of 39127c6, uncommitted when this addendum was written. Same drive (4295330750), test disc and Walkman as above. The Walkman's volume was at its minimum for the first listening (the owner confirmed it before the app was launched) and, from the session notes, for the re-test.
Lines marked "owner-reported" give the owner's answers to the questions I asked in the session; where the wording matters it is quoted. Lines marked "summary" come from the session notes, not from saved output. The app's log lines were streamed live with the commands shown and trimmed with the sed expression below: the date, process, thread and subsystem are removed, leaving time, level and category. Level Df is the default level, I is info, and E is how the app's warning-level lines appear (slow raw reads, and the line each open logs with the requested and the reported drive speed, which is not selected below). The log holds no HDCD state and no screen text, so what the screen showed and what was heard rest on the owner's reports.
CD Player was running for the listening, the re-test and the control; it was not running during the AudioCheck run (see the control).
$ TRIM='s/^[0-9-]+ ([0-9:.]+) ([A-Za-z]+) +CDPlayer\[[0-9]+:[0-9a-f]+\] \[dev\.cdplayer\.CDPlayer:([A-Za-z]+)\] /\1 \2 \3 /'

=== First listening, before the display fix (CD Player PID 95854, 19:19 to 19:37) ===
Owner-reported, summary of the answers recorded in the session notes. Stage 1, track 1 with Decode HDCD on: status line "CD DETECTED", then "HDCD PLAYING"; source text "44.1 kHz / 20-bit HDCD"; clean sound. Stage 2, Decode HDCD off on track 2 and on again on track 3: source text "44.1 kHz / 16-bit HDCD", then "44.1 kHz / 20-bit HDCD"; the decoded audio clearly quieter; clean sound. Stage 3, Stop, select track 5, Play, decoding on: the level dropped at the track 6 boundary.
Owner-reported, verbatim, the note on stage 3: "at track 5 start, there was a click sound, 16-bit HDCD, after 2 seconds, 20-bit"
My reading, from the code and not an owner report: the note points to a display bug rather than an audio fault. The engine's decoded flag was the producer's, and the producer reads ahead of playback into a 30 s ring, so on a run from track 5 it crossed the track 6 boundary (12 s into the track) seconds after Play and set the flag well before the decoded audio played. The audio side is covered by observation window B above: track 5 played undecoded and decoding began at the track 6 boundary. The note gives the text at the start as 16-bit HDCD and, 2 seconds later, 20-bit; what the text showed during the 2-second detection hold at the start of the run, in which the model keeps the previous run's state, was not pinned down.
